Hi All,
 
I want to dynamically open up a port for a Client that is behind the NAT
so that outside world can contact my client on that port. How can I do
this using iptables.
I'm using uClinux distribution for my gateway with iptablesv1.2.4. I've
only a range of ports from which I can open one port for my Client. This
port should remain open till the client is alive.
I hope iptables can do this job if not tell the possible hooks inside
the kernel for this. I'm using 2.4.18 kernel.
 
Regards,
Akhilesh
India
 
 

